7294fb7","description":"Golda Meir","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7e8c-9030-a87c0970928e","description":"Yitzhak Rabin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7325-9c6d-62276eb69437","description":"David Ben-Gurion","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7586-8a25-605ec83b104a","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which English king is traditionally said to have asked, \'Will no one rid me of this turbulent priest?\'","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Henry II\'s words are traditionally connected to Becket\'s murder by four knights in Canterbury Cathedral in 1170, though the exact wording is disputed.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-72bf-82b9-1fb6cd70ee83","description":"Henry II","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-758a-8b1a-4036158a184a","description":"William I","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-754c-8646-4674f671a715","description":"Richard III","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-72e3-bcf2-3e64b8f6d29c","description":"Henry VIII","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7e9e-8f87-e413bc64f750","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the primary language of the Aztecs?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Nahuatl is still spoken by Indigenous communities in Mexico today.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7b41-97b1-920253559bdb","description":"Nahuatl","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7595-a1b6-43ec53590999","description":"Mayan","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7f23-b371-cb5f223987cd","description":"Mixtec","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7906-baa5-83b791b0e5aa","description":"Otomi","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7a02-8d19-75cf74af8689","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the first king of Hungary?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"St. Stephen was canonized, and August 20, his feast day, is a national holiday in Hungary.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7556-ab93-c8465834add2","description":"St. Stephen","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7506-9b41-1fe7bdb9f6bf","description":"St. Marko","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-735f-941d-7a143878591b","description":"St. Cyril","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7b87-a321-fb917e691abe","description":"St. Alexander","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-78f5-8df2-e442d1e22d44","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"About how long did the American Civil War last?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The American Civil War lasted about four years, from 1861 to 1865. General Robert E. Lee\'s surrender at Appomattox in April 1865 marked a key turning point toward its end.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7d5f-a180-13c459819dad","description":"Four years","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7394-a84b-26f731c72c42","description":"One year","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7105-988e-aa871f9b0828","description":"Seven years","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7915-8cdf-d8019438e177","description":"Ten years","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-792d-8573-f3c8268facb2","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which battle was George A. Custer defeated?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"At the Battle of Little Bighorn, Lakota, Cheyenne, and Arapaho warriors overwhelmed Custer\'s forces.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-76d9-acf1-92396cb34ccd","description":"Battle of Little Bighorn","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-799f-816f-3bbe0f5073c2","description":"Battle of Gettysburg","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-792e-aa1c-c93fde29a5ad","description":"Battle of Cold Harbor","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7c52-9a0a-6d3df0c3d6d7","description":"Battle of Stones River","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-77bd-a1ba-aec09641f4cb","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the great czar who led Russia to victory against Charles XII of Sweden in The Great Northern War of 1700-1721?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Peter the Great\u2019s victory over Charles XII at the Battle of Poltava in 1709 was a turning point in the war.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7c5c-80cf-6971b6487a51","description":"Peter The Great","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7df5-ad3e-44c19084c3d2","description":"Ivan The Terrible","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-75fb-8d98-c1db789ce1fd","description":"Catherine The Great","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-75c4-b35b-017016f02192","description":"Ivan The Great","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7141-9194-ed512692b802","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which wine god\'s orgiastic worship was suppressed by the Roman Senate in the 180s BC?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Bacchus was the Roman counterpart of the Greek god Dionysus. The Senate restricted the secret rites, though worship continued under tighter controls.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7d9e-9cb6-62d3453d45a0","description":"Bacchus","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7ea0-a07c-cc428e95e8ae","description":"Apollo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7823-a912-a19c8723ed17","description":"Zeus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-79c9-b22e-7fdc5bc58555","description":"Hermes","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-70dc-9997-87e945613d8b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the name of the vehicle in which Sir Malcom Campbell broke the 300mph barrier in 1935?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Blue Bird reached 301.129 mph on Utah\'s Bonneville Salt Flats, making Campbell the first person to exceed 300 mph in a land vehicle.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7ed6-a78d-ae81f907562b","description":"Bluebird","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-764a-96cd-d322d9fccabe","description":"Dragonfly","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7168-9601-c06d405418ee","description":"Sparrow","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-763d-a5ac-b72868f1cbfc","description":"Finch","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7d88-865a-fa9384b92f95","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year was the first successful organ transplant?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The first successful organ transplant was a kidney transplant in 1954 between identical twins Ronald and Richard Herrick; their close genetic match helped limit rejection.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7f4c-b865-0b8bcb11a81c","description":"1954","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-768b-9902-42dbe2a71d17","description":"1970","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7d67-aedd-cd31d9856bf5","description":"1933","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-74b0-8aea-4956dd7166fa","description":"1981","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-782e-8755-ed03c779a577","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"The war in Vietnam ended with the fall of Saigon in what year?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The war ended in 1975; afterward, Saigon was renamed Ho Chi Minh City in honor of North Vietnam\'s revolutionary leader.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7192-8367-2e3a1bdef9a3","description":"1975","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7bb6-b0bf-5196df5e96c8","description":"1969","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-780e-882a-0da3cd286b17","description":"1980","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7464-8af0-84ce641c8006","description":"1984","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7331-b09c-9de009ac7816","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the 22nd president of the USA, in term during the period 1885\u20131889?","diffi