uring introduced by Soviet leader Mikhail Gorbachev in the 1980s?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Perestroika, meaning restructuring, began in 1986 alongside glasnost (openness) and contributed to the Soviet Union\'s collapse.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7806-9162-95df3300e71c","description":"Perestroika","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-798e-9918-0e57eb1d5d1d","description":"Apparatchik","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7fab-9040-e2fd5646f31e","description":"Uskoreniye","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7932-9f8a-f85e3dcdccd5","description":"Khozraschyot","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-73f3-b2c7-5f080517b02c","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Where did the battle of Waterloo take place?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Waterloo is in Belgium today, though the area was part of the United Kingdom of the Netherlands when the battle was fought in 1815.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7402-b0ca-3440342d7861","description":"Belgium","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-76e5-8466-1d4cc4a26742","description":"France","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7ff3-9817-2e3c05919259","description":"England","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-70b3-afbf-d7514307c4a2","description":"Italy","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7131-9fd5-0f68f7df69ba","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which ancient people carved the rose-red city of Petra?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Nabataeans made Petra the center of their kingdom and engineered channels and cisterns to manage scarce water in the desert.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-70f9-8537-fc73158352ab","description":"Nabataeans","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-788c-872a-84c581f3c833","description":"Phoenicians","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7b9d-a5c7-263ab46e4c20","description":"Babylonians","correct_answer":false},{"i