 constitution replaced the British monarch with a president as head of state, while Mintoff led the government.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-76e0-b3be-9a0bc8d1d7c6","description":"Malta","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-750d-9004-ac3e76a29ed1","description":"Cyprus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7bd2-ab4d-28ad6747e973","description":"Greece","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7c1f-abb7-98eebac40af3","description":"Spain","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-77c7-9e23-86c5db97b0ed","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"When did the United States transfer the Panama Canal to Panamanian control?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The 1977 Torrijos\u2013Carter Treaties arranged a gradual transfer, with full Panamanian control taking effect on December 31, 1999.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7f18-b537-0c96400ed207","description":"1999","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7361-be1e-2ac79470c93a","description":"1987","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-70fe-a9ff-909afb0d4d5a","description":"1991","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7bcc-a6fa-8302dfa101ad","description":"1979","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7e01-9749-66f83b300eb3","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"How many children did Queen Victoria have?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Queen Victoria had nine children with Prince Albert. Their descendants married into royal families across Europe, helping earn Victoria her nickname.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-784d-9b62-e380f1c74a0d","description":"Nine","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7266-a16d-3f56e50402c7","description":"Five","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7676-bd09-5828742d4545","description":"Seven","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7169-988c-8493814e9d6e","description":"Twelve","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7487-846d-c2