est in 1952 before reaching the summit in 1953?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Tenzing Norgay and Edmund Hillary reached the summit on May 29, 1953, and their ascent was celebrated as a joint achievement.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7744-8f32-dc2157813068","description":"Tenzing Norgay","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-756b-866f-3e4052761d49","description":"Sir Edmund Hillary","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7f8d-8e9f-4a0622b2c6d5","description":"George Mallory","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7e38-a942-0095874ab590","description":"Reinhold Messner","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-79e4-9ef9-188b5dd5f00e","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"From 1795-1806, which country was briefly known as the Batavian Republic?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Netherlands\' Batavian Republic was a French-backed successor to the Dutch Republic; in 1806, Napoleon replaced it with the Kingdom of Holland.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7c3c-adcf-f543588ee5ec","description":"The Netherlands","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7179-b42c-89cdf5a78088","description":"Poland","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7547-b474-1f3d8412042e","description":"Portugal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7555-b5e8-c73ac258185e","description":"Greece","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7467-9b34-66c3975383c3","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did the Gulf War begin?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Gulf War began in 1990 after Iraq invaded Kuwait; the U.S.-led coalition launched Operation Desert Storm the following January.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7f44-90e8-26fb0964df1d","description":"1990","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7495-878d-4405d2ea283a","description":"1983","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7b87-b351-b78ff410a40e","description":"1971","correct_a