nd is associated with the phrase \u201cThe business of America is business.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7be0-a217-b7c1533c64a9","description":"Calvin Coolidge","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7a34-9b32-436782c9ae86","description":"Martin Van Buren","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-76b1-9b56-f70003b61a94","description":"Grover Cleveland","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-70de-8034-f53fd64304d0","description":"Rutherford B. Hayes","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7df2-a5b7-5bc8a4e1906e","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In 1900, a sealed library cave holding tens of thousands of ancient manuscripts was found in which Buddhist cave complex in China\'s Gobi region?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The cache is often called the Dunhuang Library Cave. Its manuscripts include Buddhist scriptures as well as secular documents, and many are now held in institutions around the world.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-762e-9855-6ada6635710f","description":"Mogao Caves","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-732d-b62e-bd5723b8dc18","description":"Longmen Grottoes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-744b-820a-1a596ac38665","description":"Yungang Grottoes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7903-8c8f-da1294bd6aac","description":"Kizil Caves","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7fbf-8452-105869369a5c","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In 1893, which country was the first to give women the vote?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"New Zealand\u2019s 1893 Electoral Act enfranchised women, making it the first self-governing country to do so. Women could not stand for Parliament there until 1919.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7eb3-bd52-a05aaaa0a599","description":"New Zealand","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-76fb-a3ed-eca40721bbe1","description":"France","correct_answer":false},{"i