o create the \'Great Society\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Lyndon Johnson\'s Great Society included initiatives such as Medicare, federal aid to education, and the War on Poverty.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-779a-84c8-d67901cc64e8","description":"Lyndon Johnson","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-70c5-83fc-d69560c3c774","description":"Napoleon","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7b25-bdfe-4e8977158e70","description":"Oliver Cromwell","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-730b-932c-d047ce09362a","description":"Vlademir Lenin","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7a4a-b750-889d6506166a","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did Rosa Parks refuse to give up her seat in protest of racial inequality?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Parks\' arrest in 1955 helped spark the Montgomery Bus Boycott, a 381-day protest that became a major turning point in the civil rights movement.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-75bb-970d-2786e7caf877","description":"1955","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7b47-a4ad-c0861be8cd76","description":"1947","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-78fd-a867-6715a3f0fc52","description":"1963","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7ff9-bc2c-cc9d230125ef","description":"1971","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7dd0-8d96-0340eda58158","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which English King issued the Magna Carta in 1215?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"King John sealed Magna Carta at Runnymede after rebellious barons challenged his rule. The charter became an enduring symbol of limits on royal power.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7656-aaef-eef6c7301e06","description":"King John","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-77cd-b933-c46cda58f7d4","description":"King James","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7aa0-b4e6-f5946310dd0a","description":"King William","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7ecd-9a74-5cdd8014de1f","description":"King George","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-72a1-9c9d-40d0c55d40aa","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which Spanish king sent the Armada against England in 1588?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Philip II ruled Spain from 1556 to 1598. The Armada\u2019s invasion attempt failed amid English resistance and severe weather.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7902-8269-27e462fce216","description":"Philip II","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-78b7-ba42-e5f07b9c7c6b","description":"Charles V","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7a12-8d61-39dde49d7177","description":"Philip III","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-733c-9462-8374f39f4c5b","description":"Ferdinand II","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7260-8a16-c7e4ea2a5e3b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which Iranian-speaking merchant people, based around Samarkand, dominated Silk Road trade between the 4th and 8th centuries?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Sogdian merchants established trading communities along the Silk Road and connected markets in China with those farther west.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-727a-98d9-44baefec8460","description":"Sogdians","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-71dd-9821-e11766bce8fc","description":"Parthians","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-77a7-8162-83d58addda91","description":"Khazars","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7eb7-a429-b7eaa92662d7","description":"Uyghurs","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-75b6-a6cc-c1ccb32b7fa5","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Near which Egyptian city is the Valley of the Kings, the burial place of Tutankhamun?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Luxor occupies part of ancient Thebes, and the Valley of the Kings lies on the Nile\'s west bank nearby.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7e0b-9bbe-93b612d52142","description":"Luxor","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-75ed-9d10-e9cc76095065","description":"Alexandria","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7489-8317-aac89824a978","description":"Cairo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-771e-8ed7-f1e39b598b7d","description":"Port Said","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7def-90a1-1e464dd9f90d","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who is regarded as the most influential monarch of Russian Romanov Dynasty?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Peter I, known as Peter the Great, pursued sweeping military and government reforms and shifted Russia\u2019s capital from Moscow to St. Petersburg.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-75ea-b8c9-e444bf76cdae","description":"Peter I","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7620-b7c9-2d417d59aa46","description":"Nicholas III","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-77b9-b973-18b30ea636a1","description":"Ivan IV","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7aa3-bebd-1a01e72fa335","description":"Alexei VI","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7cb7-abdb-4c89c797d5bd","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which ship did Francis Drake sail around the world in 1577\u20131580?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Drake renamed the Golden Hind in honor of his patron, Sir Christopher Hatton, whose coat of arms featured a golden hind.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5529-74da-b12e-5e47f60aa762","description":"Golden Hind","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-76ac-b0c7-db90e2ef1f3a","description":"HMS Victory","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-725c-b09e-631ceb811b0b","description":"Mary Rose","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-78ea-8470-9541e4d45cc7","description":"Mayflower","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5529-7ca6-adda-5a22bcebdc49","locale":"en-US","catego